  "scope": "Four scratch-only generated AC1024 ASCII inputs with DIMSTYLE groups 41, 42, 140 and 73 omitted; ODA File Converter 27.10 Linux x86_64 generates AC1012 and reopens AC1024 ASCII DXF. The inputs vary MEASUREMENT and current HEADER dimensions independently.",
  "references": [
    "https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2023/ENU/AutoCAD-Core/files/GUID-43E31690-BA17-4AD6-82D1-E7809BD1298A.htm",
    "https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2016/ENU/AutoCAD-Core/files/GUID-60CFA531-80FD-45EF-B529-F4FAF5C758B3.htm",
    "https://ezdxf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/tables/dimstyle_table_entry.html"
  ],
  "results": [
    "All four physical DWG DIMSTYLE frames store DIMASZ=.18, DIMEXO=.0625, DIMTXT=.18 and DIMTIH=1 regardless of the input $MEASUREMENT and four current HEADER dimension settings. The four reopened DXFs omit those style groups; HEADER and MEASUREMENT match the corresponding inputs.",
    "For each frame, the versioned physical observer binds all fields and roles, rejects every byte-prefix truncation and wrong selected handle roles, and retries the unchanged frame successfully.",
    "ezdxf 1.4.5 reports 2.5, .625, 2.5 and 0 as effective values for the same omitted groups; these values are reader defaults, not explicit tags. Autodesk documents initial values for the current system variables; that does not alone establish missing DIMSTYLE group rules for arbitrary producers.",
    "An isolated red/green experiment identified that current libdxfrw uses 0 for absent DIMTIH and 1 if experimentally initialized to the ODA-observed value. Explicit 0 and 1, multiple records, binary/ASCII reads and write/re-read passed with the experimental change. The global change was not retained: without a verified way to distinguish producer/default policy it would silently alter existing 2D consumer behavior and ezdxf-style inputs.",
    "Four exact ODA DIMSTYLE records were extracted into minimal DXF wrappers, then parsed by the experimental codec, which returned the four ODA values. The full ODA-converted drawings failed this selected standalone codec import; this is not a whole-file compatibility claim."
  ],
